.TH LDASH 1 "September 2026" "ldash 1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ldash \- terminal dashboard for hledger journals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ldash
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ldash
is a real-time terminal dashboard (TUI) for
.BR hledger (1)
journals.
It renders five interactive tabs:
.TP
.B Dashboard
Forecast-aware personal finance overview: monthly income/expense breakdown
with recurring split, comparison bar chart, top expense categories, liquid
cash line chart, and YTD totals. Month navigation via
.BR h
and
.BR l .
Shown by default.
.TP
.B Accounts
All asset accounts with EUR valuations and visual bar indicators.
Enter opens the Register tab for that account (all-time history).
Savings goals are shown as progress bars.
.TP
.B Monthly
Month-by-month income and expenses bar chart with per-category breakdown,
savings rate gauge, year-over-year comparison, and category sparklines.
Enter on a category opens Register already filtered to that account.
.TP
.B Register
Postings grouped by transaction, newest first.
The query bar filters by description.
Enter opens the selected transaction's postings.
.TP
.B Portfolio
Crypto holdings table with price, value, allocation percentage, and P/L
tracking (invested vs price gain vs staking rewards).
Hidden when
.B show_portfolio
is false.
.PP
Data is loaded from
.BR hledger (1)
in the background.
The journal file is watched for changes and the dashboard reloads
automatically when it is saved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \fIFILE\fR
Path to the hledger journal file.
Overrides \fB\-\-file\fR, the config file setting, and
.BR $LEDGER_FILE .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Path to the hledger journal file.
Equivalent to the positional argument; matches hledger's
.B \-f
convention.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Path to the configuration file.
Default:
.IR ~/.config/ldash/config.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-tab " \fITAB\fR"
Start on the specified tab.
Valid values:
.BR dashboard ,
.BR portfolio ,
.BR accounts ,
.BR monthly ,
.BR register .
Overrides the
.I default_tab
setting in the config file.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the journal file and configuration, then exit without launching
the TUI.
Exits 0 on success, 1 on config/journal error, 2 if
.BR hledger (1)
is not found.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
On first launch,
.B ldash
writes a commented-out default config to
.IR ~/.config/ldash/config.toml .
The file uses TOML syntax.
Changes to most settings take effect immediately on save (hot-reload);
.I journal
and
.I default_tab
require a restart.
.SS "Top-level keys"
.TP
.B journal
Path to the hledger journal file.
Overridden by
.BR $LEDGER_FILE
and CLI flags.
.TP
.B refresh_interval
Auto-refresh interval in seconds (default:
.BR 300 ).
Ignored when the file watcher detects a change.
.TP
.B default_tab
Tab shown on startup:
.BR dashboard
(default),
.BR portfolio ,
.BR accounts ,
.BR monthly ,
or
.BR register .
.TP
.B number_format
Number formatting:
.B eu
(1.000,00) or
.B us
(1,000.00).
Default:
.BR eu .
.TP
.B currency_symbol
Currency symbol displayed in the UI (default:
.BR \(lq\(euro\(rq ).
.TP
.B chart_mode
Default portfolio chart mode:
.B stacked
(default) or
.BR unstacked .
Toggle at runtime with
.BR s .
.TP
.B show_portfolio
Boolean.
Force the Portfolio tab on or off.
Default: auto-detected from the presence of
.I assets:crypto
accounts.
.TP
.B export_format
Format for data exports:
.BR html
(default),
.BR json ,
or
.BR both .
.TP
.B export_dir
Default directory shown in the export prompt.
Default:
.IR ~/Downloads .
.SS "[colors.expenses]"
Per-category color overrides for the monthly expense table.
Keys are expense category names (case-insensitive);
values are named colors
.RB ( red ,
.BR green ,
.BR blue ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR magenta ,
.BR white ,
.BR darkgray )
or RGB hex codes
.RI ( #RRGGBB ).
.SS "[budgets]"
Monthly budget limits per expense account (case-insensitive match).
Values are floating-point amounts in the configured currency.
.nf

    [budgets]
    "expenses:Essen" = 400.0
    "expenses:Transport" = 150.0
.fi
.SS "[theme]"
Color theme settings.
.TP
.B preset
Built-in palette:
.B dark
(default),
.BR light ,
or
.BR solarized .
.TP
.BR accent ", " positive ", " negative ", " muted ", " gold ", " fg ", " background
Per-field color overrides.
Accept named colors or
.IR #RRGGBB
hex codes.
Theme changes are hot-reloaded on config save.
.SS "[[goals]]"
Savings goal entries shown as progress bars on the Accounts tab.
Each entry requires:
.TP
.B name
Display label.
.TP
.B target
Target amount (float).
.TP
.B account
Account prefix matched against your hledger accounts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ldash/config.toml
User configuration file.
Created with defaults on first launch.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/ldash.1
This man page.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TS
l l.
\fBKey\fR	\fBAction\fR
1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5	Dashboard / Accounts / Monthly / Register / Portfolio
Tab / Shift-Tab	Next / previous tab
\(ua k / \(da j	Scroll up / down; select row
PgUp / PgDn	Page up / down
Home / End	Jump to first / last row
\(<- h / \(-> l	Month (Dashboard, Monthly, Register); net worth range (Accounts); chart range (Portfolio)
G	Current month (Dashboard); latest entry (Monthly); last transaction (Register)
gg	First transaction (Register)
Enter	Open Register from account/category; open transaction legs (Register)
Esc	Back to originating tab from drilled Register; close detail; quit on direct Register
s	Toggle portfolio chart stacked / unstacked
c	Toggle expense category colors
r	Force data refresh
/	Register query bar (description filter)
i	Toggle income/expense focus (Monthly); assets/liabilities (Accounts)
p	Payee analytics (Monthly tab)
C	Year-over-year chart (Monthly tab)
F	Current-month forecast remainder (Monthly tab)
y / Y	Cycle year backward / forward (Monthly tab)
Y	Copy current view to clipboard (non-Monthly)
e	Open export prompt
?	Toggle help overlay
q	Quit
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch with a specific journal:
.EX
ldash \-\-file ~/Finance/all.journal
.EE
.TP
Use the positional argument (shorter):
.EX
ldash ~/Finance/all.journal
.EE
.TP
Use the environment variable:
.EX
export LEDGER_FILE=~/Finance/all.journal
ldash
.EE
.TP
Start on the monthly tab:
.EX
ldash \-\-tab monthly ~/Finance/all.journal
.EE
.TP
Validate config and journal without launching the TUI:
.EX
ldash \-\-check
.EE
.TP
Try the bundled sample journal:
.EX
ldash \-\-file "$(cargo locate-project \-\-message-format plain | xargs dirname)/examples/sample.journal"
.EE
.TP
Try the anonymized household demo (fake numbers):
.EX
ldash \-\-file examples/haushalt-demo/all.journal \-\-config examples/haushalt-demo/config.toml
.EE
